    intuition: 'Each correction raises the mistaken example\'s score by the square of its length (plus 1 when theta_0 is also updated). If a separator exists with some breathing room, the margin gamma, and every example has length at most R, the theorem guarantees at most (R/gamma)^2 mistakes in total. Wide gaps mean few mistakes; tight gaps mean many. If the classes overlap, fixing one example can break another, so the corrections can go on forever.',
